Six genuinely fresh independent groups pass. They execute78 exact original-helper scene/action pairs: fractional prime-denominator geometry at six scales from1/1048576 through262144; signed lines and freehand extrema; partial nested outer groups; negative-gap and equal-center overlap anchors/order; literal group-ID/shape-ID collisions; native fractional line/freehand geometry with point/pressure/unknown/app/file preservation through repeated import/export. A separate fresh group checks declared coordinate overflow rejection without caller mutation and accepted no-op ownership. Exact values, signed-zero paths and original source/mutation bindings are recorded. There is no epsilon/tolerance or numeric normalization.

The prior twelve independent groups are explicitly replays, with test/assertion bodies unchanged and only candidate/fixture import paths adapted. They pass12/12, including the previously failed fractional group. These replay bodies execute62 original-helper pairs. The separate unchanged24-packet diagnostic now passes24/24 exact. It repeats24 of those62 fixture/action pairs. Across this campaign there are164 helper calls (114align/50distribute) covering140 unique action pairs, plus two direct grouping helper calls. Overall19/19 test groups pass (6fresh+12replay+1diagnostic); they are not combined with the author's30 tests/3,968 comparisons as an independent total. The author's250-scene corpus remains author evidence.

The original source binding remains Excalidraw0.18.1, MIT, commit `a2ec2889babf7d2295469c6d90ebe77fae57df84`. Eight complete selected official source/license files are retained. The exact previously frozen independent oracle is reused unchanged: seven slices/eight declarations/five source units, three VM preparations across two owned Node children. Both original mutation helper bodies are exact. Owned dependencies are explicitly limited to unrotated rectangles/diamonds/ellipses/text or actual line/freehand point extrema, timestamp/random, undefined scene lookup, excluded elbow predicate and unbound-text/binding no-ops. Original full bounds/renderer, frame membership, bound text, native binding/rotation and original GUI are not executed. Native roundtrips are through our actual projection code; this is not full native-format/editor equivalence.

