Arithmetic remains ordinary JavaScript binary64 and source-specific operation order. The finite comparisons do not prove all values/degeneracies or improve numerical stability beyond direct extrema. Inputs retain the existing±1,000,000 coordinate/endpoint bounds,≤2,000 shapes,≤5,000 points per stroke and≤20 group levels. Layout clones/validates input and validates the output after moves; accepted input need not be closed under layout when projected origins would exceed bounds. The box helper allocates per-shape coordinate arrays and retains normal scene copies; these finite structural limits are not hard process-memory isolation or an aggregate execution-time guard. Core hit/render/SVG bounds remain unchanged.

